course: dictionary
lesson: 3148
title: Feelings words: embarrassment
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Embarrassment is the shy, silly or uncomfortable feeling you get when something happens in front of other people. Everyone feels it. Tripping on the way to the front of the class or forgetting your lines in a play can make your cheeks go hot.
explain: The word can also mean a person or thing that makes you feel this way. «Showing off to impress someone often ends with a fall or an embarrassment.» Here the fall is the thing that causes the embarrassment, so it is a noun for the thing itself.
explain: Embarrassment passes. Laughing at your own small mistakes helps, and a later sorry can put things right. Teasing others to cause embarrassment is unkind, so never do it, even as a joke.
fact: «Embarrassment» is a noun, and its plural is embarrassments.
fact: Embarrassment means feeling shy, silly or uncomfortable because of something you did, or something that happened in front of others.
fact: A person or thing that makes you feel this way can also be called an embarrassment.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «red with embarrassment», «to my embarrassment» and «cause embarrassment».
fact: Embarrassment is a normal feeling: everyone feels it sometimes, and it passes.
exercise: «Showing off to impress someone often ends with a fall or an embarrassment.» What does embarrassment mean here? | A kind of happy party | A loud shout | A thing that makes you feel shy and silly | *A thing that causes you to feel shy and silly
exercise: Tripping in front of the whole class and feeling your cheeks go hot is what kind of feeling? | Anger | Excitement | *Embarrassment | Boredom
exercise: Which is a good way to deal with embarrassment over a small mistake? | Shouting at everyone who saw it | Hiding away and never speaking again | *Laughing at your own small mistake | Teasing the person who made the mistake
test: In «He went red with embarrassment», what kind of word is embarrassment? | *A noun | An adjective | A full stop | A verb
test: Which of these is kind? | *Laughing at your own small mistakes | Teasing others to cause embarrassment | Making a friend feel embarrassed on purpose | Telling everyone a friend's secret
exam: «Shouting back when told off is often about embarrassment; a later sorry or a good deed can fix it.» What can fix the problem? | Ignoring it and hoping everyone forgets | *A later sorry or a good deed | Shouting again, louder | Blaming someone else for it
